---
/**
 * Global Storybook decorator — wraps every story so `[data-reveal]` /
 * `[data-scroll]` markup isn't stuck at `opacity: 0`.
 *
 * `global.css` ships `[data-reveal] { opacity: 0; }` and relies on
 * `initScrollAnimations()` (normally called once from `BaseLayout.astro`) to
 * tween it back in via GSAP ScrollTrigger. A component story never goes
 * through `BaseLayout`, so without this it renders invisible content that is
 * genuinely in the DOM — confusing to debug from a screenshot alone.
 *
 * This is a bare-component decorator (`decorators: [RevealDecorator]` in
 * preview.ts), the sugar form documented for Astro stories. Its own
 * `<script>` ships as part of the same rendered HTML document the story does
 * — component `<script>` tags run in the Storybook preview the same way they
 * do on the live site, they just aren't wired up by anything outside a real
 * page load, which is what this decorator stands in for.
 */
---
<slot />

<script>
  import { initScrollAnimations } from '../../src/lib/scroll-animations';
  // ScrollTrigger's own refresh on load fires `once: true` entrances that are
  // already in view, so most stories reveal immediately without scrolling.
  initScrollAnimations();
</script>
